note as N_CollectionObjectIndex
  "Collection" here is the scientific collection (Zoology, Botany, ...), distinct
  from CollectionUseProject (Collection Use context) — same English word, different
  concept. CollectionObject has no domain class in `domain/models.py` today; it
  exists only as an infrastructure/read-side concern (parser + pg_index), shown
  here to complete the data flow: collection -> source document (.xlsx) -> indexed
  row. `tsv` is a generated tsvector (config 'simple') backing full-text search.
  Staff search is broad across all indexed collections; collection filtering is
  a convenience, not row-level ACL. SourceDocument.deletedAt soft-deletes the
  document record and hard-removes its rows from the index.
  Collection catalog administration (create/rename/remove) and curator
  assign/remove are exclusive to SYS_ADMIN. There is no "inactive" state:
  removing a collection is permanent and cascades — its curator assignments,
  source documents, indexed rows, and files are all deleted, in that order.
end note
N_CollectionObjectIndex .. Collection


